@Admin @Webhooks @WebhooksStripe @WebhooksStripeSubscriptions
Feature: Handle webhook events for charge events that are generated by stripe connect

  @Seed
  Scenario: Setup test data seed for feature
    Given there are the following "subscriptions" records in the database
      | storeName                               | transactions                      | payment                                                                                                                                                                                                         | status |
      | Admin Webhooks Stripe Subscriptions One | { "rate": "0.021", "base": "10" } | { "customer": "cus_xxxxxxxxxxyyyy", "subscription": "sub_xxxxxxxxxxyyyy", "package": "TEST", "price": { "currency": "gbp", "quantity": 20, "value": 50 }, "term" : "2050-09-18T13:30:00Z", "status": "ACTIVE" } | ACTIVE |
    And there are the following "accounts" records in the database
      | identity                                         | password | status | subscription               |
      | webhooks-stripe-subscriptions-one@venzra-test.io | PASSWORD | ACTIVE | {{ subscriptions[1]._id }} |

  Scenario: A stripe payload with an invalid signature is rejected
    Given I make a POST request to the API endpoint "/admin/webhooks/stripe" as "stripe" with the mock "stripe/subscriptions/deleted-webhook.json"
    Then the status returned from the "stripe" request should be a 403 error

  Scenario: Receipt of a deleted subscription webhook from stripe
    Given there is a stripe webhook signature for the mock payload "stripe/subscriptions/deleted-webhook.json"
    When I make a POST request to the API endpoint "/admin/webhooks/stripe" as "stripe" with the mock "stripe/subscriptions/deleted-webhook.json"
    Then there should be a 200 response from the "stripe" request that contains:
      | result    |
      | OBJECT_ID |
    When I am logged in with the "webhooks-stripe-subscriptions-one@venzra-test.io" admin account
    And I make a GET request to the API endpoint "/admin/subscription" as "subscription"
    Then there should be a 200 response from the "subscription" request that contains:
      | _id       | domainName                              | additionalDomains | storeName                               | transactions                  | payment                                                                                        | addons   | status |
      | OBJECT_ID | admin-webhooks-stripe-subscriptions-one | []                | Admin Webhooks Stripe Subscriptions One | { "base": 10, "rate": 0.046 } | { "customer": "cus_xxxxxxxxxxyyyy", "term": "2020-09-18T13:37:00.000Z", "status": "CANCELED" } | ARRAY[0] | ACTIVE |
